  "provenanceNote": "A 4-cell prototype (P = 64 and 256, beta = 0 and 0.9) was run before q1-q3 were written; it gave rho(eta*) = 1 to 12 digits, so q1 and q2 were informed by it. After the predictions, a P = 16 debugging run showed that the ratio of norms does not converge on the antisymmetric part at beta = 0.9 (a cluster of eigenvalues of equal modulus), and the antisymmetric estimator was changed to the Gelfand estimate over a fixed horizon before the full run; that run gave antisymmetric radii of 0.44-0.61 at beta = 0 and about 0.906 at beta = 0.9, so q3 was seen at P = 16 before the full run. No P = 64, 256 or 1024 cell was run with the final code before the full run.",
  "predictionTexts": {
    "q1": "In every cell the radius of the second-moment operator is below 1 at (1 - 1e-3) eta* and above 1 at (1 + 1e-3) eta*, eta* the secular root of Theorem G.",
    "q2": "In every cell the crossing rho = 1, located from rho(eta*) - 1 and the local slope, is within 1e-8 (relative) of eta*.",
    "q3": "In every cell the radius on the antisymmetric matrices at eta* is strictly below 1, the radius on the symmetric part there (Lemma: the antisymmetric part never dominates)."
  },
  "predictions": {
    "q1RadiusCrossesOneAtSecularRootEveryCell": true,
    "q2CrossingWithin1e8RelativeEveryCell": true,
